# Context-scoped ignore for repo-root-context image builds
# (docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile.admin .). The context must be the repo
# root (pnpm workspace: root lockfile + the @memo/* packages admin imports),
# so this keeps the upload to manifests + sources: everything else is either
# rebuilt inside the image (node_modules, .next, dist) or irrelevant to it
# (backend, docs, e2e artifacts). Env files are excluded on purpose — Next
# loads .env* at build time and a stray local one would silently alter the
# bake; the only env that enters the build is the NEXT_PUBLIC_* build args.
.git
.worktrees
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.vercel
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json
.env*
**/.env*
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo
backend
docs
sketches
frontend/admin/e2e
frontend/admin/__tests__
frontend/admin/playwright.config.ts
frontend/admin/vitest.config.ts
# web sources are not baked into the admin image, but its package.json must
# reach the builder: pnpm resolves the whole workspace graph (frontend/*).
frontend/web/*
!frontend/web/package.json
